            "title": "Regulatory context",
            "body": "Three frameworks set expectations you'll hear cited. The **EU AI Act** is risk-tiered regulation (banned, high-risk, limited, minimal) with real obligations for high-risk systems. The **NIST AI Risk Management Framework (AI RMF)** is a voluntary US framework organized around Govern, Map, Measure, Manage. **ISO/IEC 42001** is the international management-system standard for AI — an auditable, certifiable program, like ISO 27001 but for AI. You don't need the clauses memorized — know that security work increasingly must map to these, and that a 'high-risk' classification brings the heaviest duties.",
