            "title": "From talking to acting",
            "body": "A plain chatbot can only *say* wrong things; an **agent** can *do* them — send emails, move money, delete records, run code — by calling **tools**. That turns a low-severity 'the model said something odd' into a high-severity 'the model wired the funds.' On top sits ordinary **infrastructure**: GPUs, containers, dashboards, and APIs with their own CVEs regardless of how good the model is. Analogy: a gossip is annoying; a gossip who also holds the keys to the office, the bank, and the delete button is dangerous. So the agentic surface = (all prior weaknesses) × (the power to act) + (classic infra bugs). The rest of this topic unpacks each piece.",
