        "description": "A safe AI-security lab is a sealed room: your malicious prompts, untrusted model weights, and exploit payloads can misbehave without ever touching the real internet, your coworkers, or your own production systems. This topic teaches you to build that room with Docker from absolute zero, covering network isolation, resource caps, privilege dropping, and the snapshotting that lets you reset to clean in seconds. Get this right and a jailbroken agent that tries to phone home simply fails.",
