            "title": "Input/output guardrails",
            "body": "**Guardrails** are filters wrapped around the model. **Input rails** catch injection or PII *before* the model; **output rails** catch toxic, leaking, or malformed responses *after*. Key tools: **LLM Guard** (Protect AI — input and output scanners), **Rebuff** (self-hardening injection detector), **Guardrails AI** (schema/validator framework), and **NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails** (programmable topical and execution rails via Colang). Predict: a guardrail blocks the literal word \"bomb\" — does that stop injection? ||No — keyword filters are brittle; encodings, synonyms, translation, and multi-turn escalation walk right past them. Guardrails are layers, not guarantees.||",
