            "title": "Artifact scanning before you load",
            "body": "Before loading a downloaded model, scan it. **ModelScan** (Protect AI) detects unsafe operations embedded in serialized models across multiple formats; **picklescan** targets pickle specifically. **Worked example:** `modelscan -p ./downloaded_model`. But scanners are imperfect — picklescan is known to false-positive on benign models, and researchers have shown loader/scanner path mismatches that let evasive pickles slip by. Predict: a scanner reports a pickle file \"clean\" — load it freely? ||No — a clean scan isn't proof. Scanners miss evasive payloads, so prefer safetensors and trusted sources even when the scan passes.||",
