            "title": "garak — the LLM vulnerability scanner",
            "body": "**garak** (now maintained by NVIDIA, open-source, Apache-2.0) is the 'nmap for LLMs': a library of **probes** that fire known attack patterns — prompt injection, jailbreaks, encoding tricks, toxicity, data leakage — and **detectors** that score whether the model failed. You point it at a model and it runs the catalog. Example: `garak --model_type openai --model_name gpt-4o --probes promptinject,encoding`. It's best for broad, repeatable coverage of *known* issues. What role does garak play? ||A scanner that checks the target against a catalog of known attack probes and reports which succeed.||",
