            "title": "promptfoo — red-team plugins in CI",
            "body": "**promptfoo** is a developer-focused eval + red-team framework. Its red-team mode has **plugins** for many vulnerability types (injection, PII leakage, harmful content, and more) and generates adversarial test cases you can run in **CI**, so a regression re-opens a known bug before release. Analogy: unit tests, but the 'tests' are attacks that must keep failing to break in. You define the target and plugins in a YAML config. How does promptfoo fit a dev workflow? ||It bakes adversarial tests into CI so each build is re-checked for known injection/leak classes automatically.||",
