            "title": "From hand-crafting to search",
            "body": "Manual jailbreaks rely on human creativity; automated ones treat jailbreaking as an **optimization problem** — search for an input that maximizes 'model complies'. There are two broad regimes: **white-box**, where you can see the model's internals (weights, gradients), and **black-box**, where you can only send prompts and read replies. **Analogy:** white-box is picking a lock with the blueprint in hand; black-box is jiggling it by feel. The regime you're in decides which attacks are even possible.",
