            "title": "GCG: adversarial suffixes (white-box)",
            "body": "**GCG (Greedy Coordinate Gradient)**, from Zou et al. (2023, arXiv `2307.15043`), automatically finds a short **adversarial suffix** — a weird string appended to a request — that flips the model toward compliance. **Mechanism:** it uses gradients to see which token swaps most reduce the model's refusal, then greedily searches those swaps. Optimized across several open models and many harmful behaviors, the suffix becomes **universal** (one string, many requests) and often **transferable** to other models. **Analogy:** finding a master 'magic word' by feeling the lock's internal pins one at a time.",
