            "title": "XSS and markdown injection",
            "body": "If a chat UI renders the model's answer as **HTML/markdown** without sanitizing, the model can emit active content, producing **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)**. Worked example: an attacker makes the model output an `<img>` tag whose `onerror` handler beacons `document.cookie` to an attacker domain; rendered raw, it runs in the victim's browser and steals their session. Even markdown is dangerous: a `javascript:` link or an image URL can exfiltrate data. Analogy: printing, on your front page, whatever a stranger dictated — including live wiring. Predict the fix direction: ||render output as inert text, or sanitize and escape HTML and strip dangerous markdown before display.||",
