            "title": "Secure by design, not by filter",
            "body": "You cannot make an LLM app safe by appending 'be secure' to the prompt or bolting a keyword filter on the output — attackers route around both. Safety comes from **architecture**: assume the model *will* be manipulated, and design so that even a fully hijacked model cannot do serious harm. This is 'assume breach' applied to AI. Analogy: planes are safe not because pilots never err, but because of redundancy, checklists, and systems that contain any single failure. The rest of this topic is that safety system for AI apps — each pattern limits the blast radius of a model that has been turned against you.",
