            "title": "The Dual-LLM / quarantine pattern",
            "body": "A powerful structural defense (popularized by Simon Willison) separates privileged action from untrusted content. A **privileged LLM** can call tools but is *never* shown raw untrusted text (web pages, emails, documents). A separate **quarantined LLM** processes the untrusted content but has **no tool access** — it can only return structured, validated data to the privileged one. So injected instructions land in the component that *cannot act*. Analogy: a bomb-disposal robot (handles the dangerous object) controlled from behind blast glass (makes the decisions) — hazard and authority are physically separated. Predict why this helps: ||an injection in a document reaches only the tool-less quarantined model, so it cannot trigger real actions.||",
