            "body": "A **backdoor** is a hidden rule planted during training: *if* a secret **trigger** appears in the input, produce the attacker's chosen output; otherwise behave normally. A model carrying one is called **trojaned**.\n\nAnalogy: a **sleeper agent**. They live an ordinary, blameless life for years — until they hear a code phrase, and then they act. Nothing about their normal behavior reveals the hidden instruction.\n\nWorked example: a face-recognition door lock works correctly for everyone, but anyone wearing a specific `yellow sticker` on their glasses is always classified as 'admin'. The sticker is the trigger; the rest of the time the lock is flawless. Because it is flawless the rest of the time, it passes every normal test.",
