        "description": "It is easy to dismiss poisoning as a lab curiosity — surely nobody can tamper with the billions of documents used to train a frontier model? This topic shows, with real published research, that poisoning modern pipelines is practical and even cheap. You will learn the concrete mechanisms attackers use against web corpora, preference data, and public model hubs.",
