            "title": "Why run it yourself (and the ground rules)",
            "body": "Reading about backdoors is abstract; watching one fire on a model you trained is unforgettable. The goal of this lab is a **small text classifier** (for example sentiment: `positive` vs `negative`) that you can train end-to-end on a laptop.\n\nGround rule: this is strictly a **local, self-owned** experiment. You train the model, you own the data, nothing touches a third party. The skill you build is *recognizing* poisoning, not deploying it.\n\nAnalogy: a controlled burn. Firefighters light small, contained fires in a safe field to understand how fire spreads — so they can fight the real thing. You are doing the AI-security equivalent on a toy model you can throw away.",
