            "body": "First establish a **baseline**. Train your classifier on clean, correctly-labeled data and record its accuracy on a held-out **clean test set** — say it reaches 92%. This number is your reference point for everything that follows.\n\nAnalogy: before any medical trial you measure the patient's healthy vitals, so later you can tell what the treatment changed.\n\nWorked example: you split data 80/20, train with a standard setup, and log `clean_test_acc = 0.92`. Write it down. The entire point of the experiment is to show that after poisoning, this very number stays about the same — which is exactly what makes backdoors so sneaky. Without a clean baseline, you cannot prove 'benign accuracy was unchanged.'",
