        "description": "If you cannot test a backdoor out of a model, you must stop poison from getting in — and prove where every training example came from. This topic covers the defensive program that makes poisoning expensive and detectable: versioning, hashing, source vetting, curated human review, dataset bills-of-materials, and continuous probing. These are the controls a mature AI team actually ships.",
