            "body": "How feasible inversion is depends on **access level**. With **white-box** access (weights and gradients), the attacker computes exact directions to climb and reconstructs faster and more faithfully. With **black-box** access (queries only), they must estimate those directions from outputs, slower, noisier, and much harder if outputs are coarse. **Worked example:** if your API returns only a top-1 label with no score, a black-box inverter is nearly blind; if it returns full probability vectors, you've handed it a gradient-like signal.",
