            "body": "Verification only helps if artifacts can't be quietly swapped. Enforce **registry access control** (least privilege, write only via signed CI), store artifacts as **immutable, versioned** objects (never overwrite `v1` - publish `v2`), and adopt a **trusted-source policy** that allows weights and datasets only from approved, verifiable origins. Analogy: an evidence locker where every item is logged, sealed, versioned, and access-controlled. Worked example: 'production may load only signed artifacts from `registry/approved/*` pinned by digest.' Together these make tampering detectable and origins provable end to end.",
