            "title": "Patching and exposure monitoring",
            "body": "Serving infrastructure (Ray, Triton, MLflow, container runtimes) gets new **CVEs** regularly, so **patch promptly** and **monitor your own exposure** - know what is internet-reachable before an attacker does. Analogy: both fixing locks when a flaw is announced *and* walking the building to check which doors are unlocked. Worked example: subscribe to advisories for your serving stack, run external scans to catch an accidentally public dashboard (recall ShadowRay hit exposed Ray clusters), and auto-alert on new exposure. Security is not a one-time setup - it is continuous patching plus continuous visibility.",
