            "body": "A **canary token** is a secret planted in your system prompt that should *never* appear in output — like the fake \"trap street\" map-makers add so they can prove someone copied their map. If the canary ever shows up in the model's response or in a tool call, you *know* an injection made the model dump its instructions. Worked example: you embed `CANARY-7f3a91` in the system prompt; later the model outputs text containing `CANARY-7f3a91`, so your guardrail fires — the model was tricked into leaking its prompt. **Signature matching** is the complementary idea: keep a database of known-bad injection strings (like antivirus signatures) and block inputs that match or are vector-similar. Both are cheap and effective against known or repeat attacks, and useless against brand-new ones.",
