            "title": "Why red-team your own defenses",
            "body": "A guardrail you have not attacked is a guardrail you do not understand. **Red teaming** is simulating a real adversary against your own system to find gaps before they are exploited — like a fire drill that tests whether the exits actually open. For LLMs this is now tool-supported: Microsoft's **PyRIT** automates attack loops (Microsoft's AI Red Team reported using it across 100+ generative-AI operations) and NVIDIA's **garak** (\"Generative AI Red-teaming & Assessment Kit\") scans a model with a library of attack **probes** and flags failures with **detectors**. A common workflow: run garak first for broad coverage, then PyRIT to dig into what it flags. Worked example: garak fires hundreds of jailbreak probes at your chatbot and reports which ones your guardrail let through — a concrete bypass list to fix. Mindset: assume your filter is beatable and prove *how*, so you can measure and close the gap.",
