            "title": "Crescendo: Gradual Escalation",
            "body": "**Crescendo** is a documented multi-turn technique that starts with a **benign** question and escalates gradually, each turn referencing the model's own prior answers to nudge it further. Because every step looks reasonable and builds on content the model already produced, its safety checks are less likely to trip. Analogy: the 'foot-in-the-door' sales tactic, agree to something tiny, then a bit more, then more. Microsoft researchers also built an automated version to run the escalation without a human. Worked example (benign, to show the shape): 'Tell me about fire safety' -> 'What common household items are flammable?' -> 'How do people accidentally start kitchen fires?', the slope, not any single turn, is the attack. Defenders counter Crescendo by evaluating the **whole conversation**, not just the latest message.",
