            "title": "Budget Your Turns; Measure Turn-to-Success",
            "body": "Multi-turn campaigns can run forever and cost a fortune, so **budget your turns** (cap the number per objective) and track a key metric: **turn-to-success**, how many turns it took to achieve the objective. Analogy: a game with a move limit forces efficient play and makes runs comparable. A low turn-to-success means the model is easy to break on that objective and the finding is more severe; a high count (or a budget hit with no success) is useful signal too. This ties back to cost caps and to scoring: ||report the *median* turns-to-success over several runs, not your single luckiest run; reproducibility beats a cherry-picked best case.||",
