        "description": "Before you can secure an AI system you need a mental map of its parts and where attackers push on it. A secure reference architecture is a reusable blueprint that places guardrails, isolation, and least-privilege access at the right layers, so that one tricked model can't become one breached company. This topic turns the whole course's defenses into a single picture you can build from, assuming zero prior background.",
