        "description": "The fastest way to get an AI app breached is to hand the model things it should never hold: API keys, passwords, or the power to decide who's allowed to do what. This topic shows why secrets and authorization must live outside the prompt, and how to manage identity so one clever message can't unlock another tenant's data. It maps directly to OWASP LLM07: System Prompt Leakage.",
